 ## Overview
-SA-GS is a 3D Gaussian Splatting variant that incorporates semantic masks and geometric complexity constraints to refine Gaussian shapes and reduce the number of splats, thereby improving geometric reconstruction quality and reducing GPU memory consumption [S1, unofficial]. It differs from vanilla 3DGS by adding semantic-aware shape constraints (disk-like for low frequency, stick/dot for high frequency) and alpha-based point extraction instead of using Gaussian means directly [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Spectrum and Edge-based Gaussian Splat Count Estimation](19432-spectrum-and-edge-based-gaussian-splat-count-estimation.md) by using spectral complexity to determine expected Gaussian counts per semantic group.
